<a name="toc_tc70125"></a><p>&nbsp;</p><div> <table class="tc" width="90%" ><tr><th colspan="4">Test Case CTCP-4404: Verify download pdf functionality&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 80%;">[Version  : 1]</span></th></tr>
<tr><td width="20%" valign="top"><span class="label">Author:</span></td><td colspan="3">uig84184</td></tr>
<tr><td width="20%" valign="top"><span class="label">Last edit by:</span></td><td colspan="3">uie_32437</td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="4"><span class="label">Summary:</span><br />Verify download pdf functionality</td></tr><tr><td colspan="4"><span class="label">Preconditions:</span><br />Following data should be created for inspection 
1. Corporate CV1
2. Site S1
3. Conveyor CV1, CV2
4. Inspection event- Multi inspect 
5. Item with conveyor CV1
Item1.1 -To be completed, Good 
Item1.2 -To be completed, Critical 
Item1.3 -To be completed, Fault 
Item1.4 -To be completed, Fault 
6. Item with conveyor CV2
Item2.1 -Completed, Good 
Item2.2 -Completed, Critical 
Item2.3 -To be completed, Fault 
Item2.4 -To be completed, Fault </td></tr><tr><td><span class="label">#:</span></td><td><span class="label">Step actions:</span></td><td><span class="label">Expected Results:</span></td></tr><tr><td width="5">1</td><td>Based on precondition data download inspection Multi inspect </td><td>User should able to download the inspection event </td></tr><tr><td width="5">2</td><td>Look for the file name of the pdf report</td><td>The pdf report should generate with name :
Inspection date(2025-01-21-)+Sitename(testVMCSIte@9)</td></tr><tr><td width="5">3</td><td>Look for heading displayed on the top of pdf report</td><td>The pdf report should display inspection event name : 21. Jan, 2025 testVMCSIte@9</td></tr><tr><td width="5">4</td><td>Look for generated date </td><td>Generated date should display the date PDF report is generated egg :Generated Date: Jan 23, 2025</td></tr><tr><td width="5">5</td><td>Look for generated by</td><td>Generated by should display the name of user who downloaded the report</td></tr><tr><td width="5">6</td><td></td><td>Inspection table should display :
-Inspection date, Site & Inspector in data</td></tr><tr><td width="5">7</td><td>Look for data displayed in overview graph </td><td>The overview graph should display : Total, Critical, Fault & Good card with respective item count
To be completed will also be reflected with respective color of conditions </td></tr><tr><td width="5">8</td><td>Look for condition and status count table </td><td>Following column should display : 
1. Conveyor name CV1 & CV2
2. Critical column with Completed and To be completed count 
3. fault column with Completed and To be completed count 
4. Good column with Completed and To be completed count 
The count should in table should match with inspection event details count
</td></tr><tr><td width="5">9</td><td>Look for items displayed for respective conveyor inspections </td><td>respective conveyor should display the following details :
Inspections-CV1
Table [ Belt width, Belt carcass, Belt Rating, Top & Bottom cover thickness ]</td></tr><tr><td width="5">10</td><td>Look for details displayed for each inspection item</td><td>Following details should show :
Conveyor name, Asset, Detail, Recommendation, Observation, Status & Condition 
If any image is uploaded with item it should also display</td></tr><tr><td width="5">11</td><td>Look for Conveyor inspection item display sequence in report</td><td>The order sequence should be same as it displays in front end event details page </td></tr><tr><td width="5">12</td><td>Look for the data displayed in footer of the page </td><td>Footer of the pdf page should display :
- Continental AG 2025. All Rights Reserved.
-Pagination entry</td></tr><tr><td width="20%" valign="top"><span class="label">Execution type:</span></td><td colspan="3">Manual</td></tr>
<tr><td width="20%" valign="top"><span class="label">Estimated exec. duration (min):</span></td><td colspan="3"></td></tr>
<tr><td width="20%" valign="top"><span class="label">Importance:</span></td><td colspan="3">High</td></tr>
